> What do you do with a .diff

You apply it to the source code (before you compile it) with the program
"patch".

Btw: A .diff file is actually just a list of differences between
different text-files. In case of patches the files show the differences
between the vanilla source code and the source code with the added
functionality. The program patch just applies these changes.

